I really struggled earlier with how to  sort of present this story to you so  that it would transmit the true  absurdity that it represents so maybe  the best place to start is with some  basics like for example the federal  deficit has been skyrocketing under  Donald Trump the federal deficit is up  nearly a third 32% in the first 11  months of fiscal 2018 over fiscal 2017  up about two hundred and twenty-two  billion dollars this is according to the  nonpartisan Congressional Budget Office  why is the deficit up well the  Republican tax law is part of the  problem and increases in spending are  part of the problem if you reduce tax  revenues and you increase spending your  deficit is going to go up nothing  mathematically complicated about that  what is expected to happen next year and  the year after more of the same the same  Congressional Budget Office estimates  that we are going to have more deficit  growth in 2019 fiscal year 2019 and then  even more beyond that in fiscal year  2020  so first of all let me make very clear  this is not a conversation about whether  deficits matter and how much they matter  we've talked a lot in the last year and  a half to two years about modern  monetary theory and the growing reality  that a dollar of deficit is not always  the same for the economy the deficit  spending on stuff that stimulates the  economy is good right it's not or at  least it's not necessarily bad but on  the other hand growing the deficit to  give rich people tax cuts that they will  put mostly in bank accounts is not good  for the economy but that's not what I  want to talk about today right we've got  that part down we've talked about that  many times Donald Trump ran on reducing  the deficit and on paying down the  national debt the exact opposite is  what's actually happening but I think  even more importantly than that we got  these new deficit numbers the day after  we found out that when former Trump  economic adviser Gary cone went to trump  and said mister  whatever he calls a mr. president who  cares whatever name he had for him he  said Donald Donny boy the federal funds  rate is going to go up Donald Trump had  the bright idea of starting to print  more money in order to then make money  by holding US currency which he would  just print now you can debate whether  that's a good idea  but Trump and Republicans have run for  decades on economic theory that  supposedly claims that you can't do that  that that is inflationary and that it is  an absolute economic disaster to do that  what we have learned from this  experiment are a few different things  number one Trump and Republicans don't  care about the deficit I've been saying  this for a while it's a political  football the deficit matters when Barack  Obama is in office I'd say when Bill  Clinton's in office although he had a  surplus at the end of his presidency but  when george w bush is in office or  donald trump is in office who could  deficit who cares about the deficit  we're cutting taxes for the rich and for  big corporations deficit i don't even  know what you're talking about that's  what we learned number one even though  we already probably knew that number two  and this is not a new theme donald trump  has no idea how money works I'm not  talking about economics he obviously has  no idea how economics works he doesn't  seem to understand how money works and  then thirdly and this is the really sort  of damaging important stuff  Republicans will then use the fact that  these deficits exist because they gave  tax cuts to the rich to support more bad  policy by saying listen we've got  deficits we've got to cut Medicare and  we've got to cut Social Security  benefits even though they caused the  problem I jokingly what was that phrase  I've been using about the Trump  administration solutions that don't work  two problems that don't exist  this is solutions that don't work two  problems you caused and that's when it  starts to ruin people's lives in a real  way and again I know people are going to  write to me because every time I talk  about debt and deficit people write in  with two different  basically two different themes number  one people write in clearly  misunderstanding the difference between  debt and deficit I'm not going to review  that today we've already talked about  that before the other one is I get  emails from people saying David you  don't still think the deficit matters do  you and the answer is well the deficit  does matter but what modern monetary  theory is increasingly illuminating is  that a dollar of deficit is not always  created equal and what matters is why  did we get into that deficit dollar in  the first place was it to give a rich  person another dollar to stash away in  their bank accounts in a totally non  economically stimulative way or did that  dollar go to give someone health care  who now by virtue of being healthier is  going to work more and make more money  and the government gets more money  because they're earning income taxes or  collecting income taxes and that person  now has more money to go out and spend  it at local businesses that's what  matters okay so if you're gonna write in  and say David the deficit doesn't matter  at all  I've not seen evidence to suggest it  doesn't matter at all but what I am  increasingly convinced of is that what  matters is how did we get into that  deficit over the long term if you're not  following the david pakman show on  instagram you're missing a lot of really  great stuff including david pakman show  videos on IG TV we are on instagram at  david pakman show please follow us there  and make sure you're also following me  if you want to see behind the scenes  pictures from my trip and everything  that I've been doing over the last  couple of weeks follow me on Instagram  at David Pakman we will take a quick  break part two of my interview with  Andrew Seidel from the Freedom From  Religion Foundation next then more  stories and a lot of really great stuff  coming up today
 

